{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Also</b>, <b>despises</b>, <b>are not</b> — three connected words." "The word <b>also</b> — inclusive, and it is connected above with <b>a man of schemes</b>. And likewise it is: when a man hates evil thoughts, <b>also</b> he who despises his fellow hates the poor man, on account of his poverty." "<b>And the friends of the rich are many</b> — on account of his wealth they are many. And whoever despises his fellow who is worthy of honor — he is a sinner."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:47.690501418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}